{"resource":{"id":"rust-beginner-guide","title":"Rust \u2014 Beginner Guide","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"17 min","pages":22,"lastUpdated":"March 2026","tags":["Programming","Rust","Systems"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"A gentle introduction to Rust \u2014 ownership, borrowing, types, control flow, structs, enums, modules, and error handling explained with analogies."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Why Rust?"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Installation & Hello World"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Variables & Data Types"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Control Flow"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Functions"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Ownership"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Borrowing & References"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Structs"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Enums & Pattern Matching"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Modules & Crates"},{"id":"s11","label":"11. Error Handling"},{"id":"s12","label":"12. Rust Philosophy"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Rust \u2014 Complete Tutorial","tag":"Programming","time":"41 min"},{"title":"Rust \u2014 Step-by-Step Learning Guide","tag":"Programming","time":"24 min"},{"title":"Rust \u2014 Cheat Sheet","tag":"Programming","time":"5 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Understand what makes Rust unique \u2014 safety without a GC.</li>\n          <li>Write, compile, and run simple Rust programs.</li>\n          <li>Grasp ownership and borrowing with everyday analogies.</li>\n          <li>Read idiomatic Rust code with confidence.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Why Rust?</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Rust delivers C-level performance with memory safety guaranteed at compile time. No null pointers, no data races, no garbage collector. It powers Firefox, Cloudflare, Discord, and parts of the Linux kernel.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-sky-500/40 bg-sky-500/10 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 16v-4\"/><path d=\"M12 8h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Analogy</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Think of Rust as a strict but helpful editor who catches bugs before they ship \u2014 the borrow checker is your co-author.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Installation &amp; Hello World</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>curl --proto &#x27;=https&#x27; --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh\ncargo new hello &amp;&amp; cd hello &amp;&amp; cargo run</code></pre></div>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fn main() {\n    println!(&quot;Hello, world!&quot;);\n}</code></pre></div>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 \u2014 The Rust toolchain: rustup manages toolchains, cargo manages projects, rustc compiles.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Variables &amp; Data Types</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Variables are immutable by default. Use <code>mut</code> to opt in to mutability.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>let x = 5;          // immutable\nlet mut y = 10;     // mutable\nlet name: &amp;str = &quot;Ada&quot;;\nlet age: u32 = 30;\nlet pi: f64 = 3.14;\nlet is_ok: bool = true;</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Control Flow</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>if x &gt; 0 { println!(&quot;positive&quot;); } else { println!(&quot;non-positive&quot;); }\nfor i in 0..5 { println!(&quot;{}&quot;, i); }\nlet mut n = 3;\nwhile n &gt; 0 { n -= 1; }</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Functions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fn add(a: i32, b: i32) -&gt; i32 {\n    a + b // last expression is the return value\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Ownership</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Every value has a single owner. When the owner goes out of scope, the value is dropped. This eliminates a whole class of memory bugs.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>let s = String::from(&quot;hi&quot;);\nlet t = s;          // s is moved into t\n// println!(&quot;{}&quot;, s); // ERROR: s no longer valid</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Borrowing &amp; References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Instead of moving, you can borrow \u2014 either shared (<code>&amp;T</code>) or mutable (<code>&amp;mut T</code>). Rules: many shared XOR one mutable.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fn len(s: &amp;String) -&gt; usize { s.len() }\nlet s = String::from(&quot;hi&quot;);\nprintln!(&quot;{}&quot;, len(&amp;s)); // s still owned here</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Structs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>struct User { name: String, age: u32 }\nlet u = User { name: &quot;Ada&quot;.into(), age: 30 };</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Enums &amp; Pattern Matching</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>enum Shape { Circle(f64), Square(f64) }\nmatch s {\n    Shape::Circle(r) =&gt; 3.14 * r * r,\n    Shape::Square(a) =&gt; a * a,\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Modules &amp; Crates</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>A crate is a compilation unit; a module organises code within a crate. <code>Cargo.toml</code> lists dependencies (external crates).</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 \u2014 Rust crate/module hierarchy: workspace \u2192 crate \u2192 module \u2192 item.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Error Handling</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Two flavours: <code>Result&lt;T, E&gt;</code> for recoverable errors, <code>panic!</code> for unrecoverable ones. Use <code>?</code> to propagate errors concisely.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fn read() -&gt; Result&lt;String, std::io::Error&gt; {\n    let s = std::fs::read_to_string(&quot;f.txt&quot;)?;\n    Ok(s)\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">12. The Rust Philosophy</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Make invalid states unrepresentable.</li>\n          <li>Fearless concurrency: the compiler proves data-race freedom.</li>\n          <li>Zero-cost abstractions: high level, no runtime overhead.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Rust's power comes from ownership + borrowing. Once those click, everything else \u2014 traits, lifetimes, async \u2014 builds on top.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is Rust hard?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Steeper than most, gentler than C++. Expect a two-week ramp.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Do I need to know C?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No, but familiarity with pointers helps.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Ownership</strong> \u2014 each value has exactly one owner at a time.</li>\n          <li><strong>Borrow</strong> \u2014 a reference that doesn't take ownership.</li>\n          <li><strong>Crate</strong> \u2014 Rust's compilation and distribution unit.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Educational content. Verify against the current Rust edition.</p>\n      </div></section>"}